{
  "_about": "Best known starting values per printer model and filament kind. Keys: the machine as its slicer profile names it (FarmPrinter::machineName(), lower case substring) -> kind code -> finish (or '*'). Values have the shape of farm_printer_materials.overrides. Since 17 Oct 2026 (Roman): the material decides the temperatures and the flow (Matplace spools print close to Bambu Lab's numbers: PLA 220, PLA+ 220, silk 230, matte 220, PETG 255), the machine decides the cooling, the volumetric cap, the retraction and the pressure advance (Anycubic Slicer Next 7/2026 profiles for the Kobra S1 and the Kobra 3 Max). Temperatures here win over the kind's own: the same kind runs hotter beds on the Max. Only what differs from the machine's own filament profile (engines/orca/profiles) is written here. A tuned row on the same machine profile with the same nozzle beats these. Everything is written for a 0.4 mm nozzle: a machine with another nozzle takes its flow rates and speeds from its own slicer profiles instead. `_materials` carries the kind-level temperatures (the S1 numbers) for farm:library-refresh --kinds.",
  "_materials": {
